// [draft]
=== recipe_shelf ===
I shelved the book and looked again at the torn-out page. “Knafeh Im Khalil”… and then nothing. #salma #thinking
Look at the edge: straight, really neat. This didn't tear by accident. #lana
So [[Teta]] tore it out herself… but why? #salma
Nobody tears out a page like that to throw it away. You tear it out to leave it with someone you trust. #lana
-> END

// [draft]
=== knafeh_station ===
The first tray from the knafeh station: the cheese is salty, and the bottom is burnt. #sys
No, no, keep going. I'm only watching. #abu_fadi #smile
Uncle, what's wrong with it? Just tell us. #lana
I promised to drink my coffee and keep quiet. But the cheese… it needs to soak overnight. #abu_fadi
So we try again tomorrow. #salma #smile
-> END

// [draft]
=== abu_fadi_chair ===
Your chair, Abu Fadi. I tightened the legs and didn't change a single piece of wood. A chair knows its owner. #karim
Your Teta told me: when both my girls' girls are under one roof… #abu_fadi #thinking
Then what? #lana #surprised
The roof is mended, and you two sat at one table and decided together. It's time. #abu_fadi
Time for what, Uncle? #salma
Tomorrow morning. Bring two cups, and come to the window. #abu_fadi
-> END

// [draft]
=== window_seat ===
Abu Fadi took an old envelope from his pocket and set it down between them. #sys
In 2006 she gave it to me whole. In 2019 she took it back for one night, and returned it like this… in strips. #abu_fadi
Why did she tear it up, Uncle? #salma
She said: whoever wants to read it must sit down and put it together by hand. Like coffee. #abu_fadi
And you? Twenty years, and you never read it? #lana #sad
I promised her, my girl. #abu_fadi
-> END

// [draft]
=== book_case ===
The old books are in the case, and the page lies on the table in strips. Lana called her mother. #sys
Mom, pick up… I just want to ask you one thing. #lana
The phone rang and rang. No answer. #sys
Mine too… she always knows when I'm about to ask, and she doesn't pick up. #salma #sad
Fine. We'll put it together ourselves, and take it to them. #lana
-> END

// [draft] Faris's apology, with the callback for c8_offer (see chapter9.ink).
=== the_page ===
Before they could put the page together, Faris walked in. No suit, no business smile. #sys
{
- chose("faris_table") == "hear":
    You heard me out to the end, and I didn't tell you everything. I'm sorry. #faris #sad
- else:
    You asked me to leave, and you were right. I'm sorry. #faris #sad
}
I asked my father about the agreement. He said one thing: “She didn't haggle. Not one piastre.” #faris
Teta? She didn't haggle? #salma #surprised
The offer's withdrawn. Whatever the papers say. #faris
Come on, Salma. Let's put the page together, and put it under glass. #lana
-> END

// Memory 9 (reassemble): the torn knafeh page; its back is letter_5.

// [draft]
=== m9_lead ===
Do you know who was the first to taste this knafeh? #abu_fadi #smile
Summer of '74. I was sitting by the window, and the smell drifted out into the street… #abu_fadi
-> END

// [draft]
=== m9_intro ===
Fadi! Come and taste this, and tell me the truth. No flattery. #teta_young
Knafeh? In a café? Since when, Um Khalil? #fadi_young #surprised
Since today. If you like it. #teta_young #smile
-> END

// [draft] The page's front, one strip per line in the right order.
=== m9_page ===
Knafeh Im Khalil #letter
A pound of Nabulsi cheese, soaked in water overnight. #letter
Rub the fine knafeh dough with ghee until it's like sand. #letter
Half of it in the tray, the cheese on top, then the other half. #letter
A low flame, and keep turning the tray. Knafeh is like coffee: it needs patience. #letter
Cold syrup on hot knafeh, with one cardamom pod in it. That's the secret. #letter
— Um Khalil, summer '74. Witness: Fadi, who ate two plates. #letter_signature
-> END

// [draft]
=== m9_perfect ===
Um Khalil… this isn't knafeh. This is Eid. #fadi_young #surprised
-> END

// [draft]
=== m9_ok ===
Something's still missing… but we'll get there. #teta_young #thinking
-> END

// [draft]
=== m9_outro ===
Write me the recipe, Um Khalil. I want to make it for my mother. #fadi_young
The recipe goes in my book, and there it stays. This one is never sold, and never given away. #teta_young #smile
Thirty-two years later, the page was torn out of the book. #sys
-> END

// [draft]
=== m9_return ===
Salma… there's writing on the back of the page. In Teta's hand. #lana #surprised
That's not mine to read. I'll drink my coffee outside. #abu_fadi
They laid the page on the counter, by the drawer, and read its back together. #sys
-> END

// [draft] Letter 5, the back of the page, to Rana and Nawal.
=== letter_5 ===
Rana, Nawal, my hearts, #letter
In 2006 we were drowning in debt, and Faris's father wanted my knafeh and its name. #letter
I refused in public, then sold them for ten years in secret. I was ashamed. #letter
Nawal drew up the papers, as witness. I swore her to silence, even with her sister. #letter
Rana, Nawal sold nothing. I was the one who told you: ask your sister. #letter
I tore this page out so it can never be sold again, and I'm paying back every coin. #letter
2019: paid in full. The agreement is over. Not one stone of this café is theirs. #letter
— Your mother #letter_signature
-> END

// [draft]
=== voice_5 ===
My heart… if you've read it, take it to your mothers. I couldn't. #teta
-> END

// [draft]
=== notify_5 ===
Got the photo, Lana. Twenty years I kept quiet… I've just booked a flight to Amman. #nawal
-> END
